    ],
    "expectedRule": "Chapter 1 fog pressure (0-3). A first clear of a monster or trap that dealt damage raises fog by 1; clearing the relief nodes sealed_cache or quiet_prayer_reward, or succeeding at the relief events blood_rune_stair or mist_sealed_cache, lowers it by 1; an event outcome that deals damage raises it by 1; the result is clamped to 0-3. Display: title 妖雾压境, status `雾压 n/3`, severity stable at 0, warning at 1, danger at 2-3, meter {n, 3}, targetReached at 0. Encounter allStatsPercent is +10 at fog 2 and +20 at fog 3. With mist_breathing as the main method every trap is seen through, so a risked trap deals max(4, floor(damage x 0.45)): blood_rune_trap 24 -> 10, ash_pit_trap 19 -> 8. blood_rune_stair: send_pet_first without a trap-scout pet fails for 20 damage; breathe_through_runes succeeds with mist_breathing and deals none; mist_sealed_cache match_cache_breath likewise succeeds. A resolved event is rejected the second time. Gate demon_clear_blood_stair (blood_rune_trap -> left_watch_trap) needs fog 0 and while closed reads `雾压需降至 0 或以下；先去雾后暗格或静默香案减压。`; the move is then not a legal destination. The fog_lesser_demon (42 HP) outlives the first strike of the starting blade, and a surviving monster always lands at least 1 damage, so its first clear raises fog. Chapter 1 entered for the first time carries no lantern, so no pursuer interrupts the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
